cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research compendium, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "$PKG_NAME"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "$DATE"
license: $LICENSE_TYPE
authors:
  - family-names: $AUTHOR_FAMILY_NAME
    given-names: $AUTHOR_GIVEN_NAME
    orcid: ""
    email: $AUTHOR_EMAIL
    affiliation: $AUTHOR_AFFILIATION
# Edit the abstract to describe this compendium. Say what it does and does
# not contain: restricted or third-party data are often withheld, and the
# data availability statement says how to obtain them.
abstract: >
  Research compendium created with zzcollab v$ZZCOLLAB_TEMPLATE_VERSION:
  the code and computational environment for the analyses. See the data
  availability statement for which data are included and how to obtain
  any that are not.
keywords:
  - reproducible-research
  - research-compendium
